Both lines 121–122 are inside the PROBE template literal (which starts around line 113 with `const PROBE = \`(async () => {`). So the probe now contains these lines as JS inside the page — `console.log('RAW RESULT:', JSON.stringify(r)...)` — `r` is not defined in the page... and `const r = await send(...)` — `send` is not defined in the page → the probe will throw an exception.

This is getting out of hand. The edit tool's line anchors are unreliable here (file was rewritten, and tags are going stale). The cleanest path: completely rewrite the file with `write` (which I know works) — this time making sure there are no typos, and including the raw dump. Then run it.

Lesson: after `write`, don't re-anchor edits based on a stale read; if changes are needed, re-read first.

